    "body": "Yeah sure that makes perfect sense. AFAIK if both a `[tool.poetry]` and a `[project]` table are present then it's an invalid `pyproject.toml` so I think in that case it's fine for starship not to show either?\r\n\r\nI think poetry is the last modern python build backend that does not support PEP 621 so there should be no reason for a user to combine the two formats, and if/when poetry starts to support PEP 621 then the `[tool.poetry]` section will disappear in favour of `[project]` anyway",
    "created_at": "2022-05-01T09:20:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-01T11:57:39Z",
